The '''Namadii Corridor''' was a [[hyperspace route]] that ran from the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] in [[the Interior]] and [[Core Worlds]] region of [[the galaxy]] to the astronomical object [[Namadii system|Namadii]] in the [[Mid Rim Territories]]. It passed through the [[Colonies]], [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]], and [[Expansion Region]] on its route with junctions onto various other routes including the [[Corellian Run]] and the [[Perlemian Trade Route]].

==Description==
The Namadii Corridor was a [[hyperspace route]] that had one terminus at the [[Galaxy|galactic]] [[capital]] [[Coruscant]] in the [[Coruscant system]] of the [[Corusca sector]]'s [[Coruscant subsector]] in the [[Core Worlds]]<ref name="COTR" /> and [[the Interior]] regions of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Interior" /> From there, it connected to the astronomical objects [[Pantolomin system|Pantolomin]] and [[Borleias]]<ref name="GM" /> of the [[Borleias system]],<ref name="Alphabet" /> both also in the Core Worlds, and then astronomical object [[Palanhi system|Palanhi]] in the [[Colonies]].<ref name="GM" />

Next, the route entered the [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]] and passed through the astronomical objects [[Marquinn]],<ref name="GM" /> the [[gas giant]]<ref name="Poe Dameron 7">[[Poe Dameron 7|''Poe Dameron'' 7]]</ref> [[Pheryon]], and<ref name="GM" /> the [[Planet|world]]<ref name="Leia">''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]''</ref> [[Bilbringi]]. After entering the [[Expansion Region]], it linked to<ref name="GM" /> the [[Kel Dor]] [[homeworld]]<ref name="Aliens">''[[Star Wars: Aliens of the Galaxy]]''</ref> [[Dorin]] and then finally it entered the [[Mid Rim Territories]] and passed through<ref name="GM" /> the [[Nautolan]] homeworld<ref name="Glee Anselm">{{Databank|glee-anselm|Glee Anselm}}</ref> [[Glee Anselm]]<ref name="GM" /> in the [[Jalor sector]]'s<ref name="Jango Fett 1" /> [[Jalor system]],<ref name="Obi-Wan & Anakin" /> then<ref name="GM" /> the planet<ref name="Helmet Collection 73">{{HelmetCollectionCite|73|Databank A-Z}}</ref> [[Ansion]], and finally reached its other terminus at the astronomical object [[Namadii system|Namadii]]. On the [[Standard Galactic Grid]], Namadii Corridor passed through squares K-10, K-9, K-8, J-8, J-7, I-7, and I-6.<ref name="GM" />

Coruscant acted as a junction from the Namadii Corridor onto the [[Corellian Run]],<ref name="COTR" /> [[Metellos Trade Route]],<ref name="Metellos" /> [[Perlemian Trade Route]],<ref name="COTR" /> [[Stassia Alley]],<ref name="Stassia" /> and the [[Koros Trunk Line]], which was part of the larger [[Nexus Route]].<ref name="Koros" /> A route also passed from Coruscant out to the Core Worlds planet Chandrila, with another route then looping back from Chandrila to meet the Namadii Corridor at Pantolomin. Palanhi served as a junction between the Corridor and<ref name="GM" /> the [[Shwuy Exchange]],<ref name="Shwuy" /> Dorin as a junction on to the [[Celanon Spur]], and Ansion onto a route that eventually led to the world [[Benath]].<ref name="GM" />

==Behind the scenes==
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the Namadii Corridor was first pictured in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 18|eighteenth]] issue of the ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' magazine,<ref name="BMF18">{{BuildFalconCite|18|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> published around [[May 6]], [[2015]].<ref name="BMFdate">{{BuildFalconDates|36}}</ref> It was first identified in ''[[Collapse of the Republic]]'', a [[2019]] ''[[Star Wars Roleplaying]]'' supplement published by [[Fantasy Flight Games]].<ref name="COTR" />

The [[Namadii Corridor/Legends|Namadii Corridor]] originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it first appeared in the [[2000]] novel ''[[The New Jedi Order: Agents of Chaos I: Hero's Trial]]'', which was written by [[James Luceno]].<ref name="AOC1">''[[The New Jedi Order: Agents of Chaos I: Hero's Trial]]''</ref> It was then depicted for the first time in ''[[The Essential Atlas]]'', a [[2009]] reference book written by [[Daniel Wallace]] and [[Jason Fry]].<ref name="TEA">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref>

